    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0674" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11035: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-09T17:00:00+08:00">November 9, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 9—5:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>738. Embassy’s 735, November 8, 4 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The local Japanese spokesman has announced that the Japanese occupation of
                        Taiyuan was completed this morning.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Press reports indicate that Changteh in northern Honan on the
                        Peiping–Hankow Railroad is now occupied by the Japanese (Embassy’s 728,
                        November 5, 4 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d729-f1"/>)</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, by courier to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
